### Privacy Policy for SurgTech Gemini Library

**Effective Date:** November 08, 2025  
**Contact:** morgrum@gmail.com

---

#### 1. Overview  
SurgTech Gemini Library (the “Application”) consists of:
- The Moodle User Interface Chrome extension
- The SurgTech Gemini Library desktop automation tool

These tools are used solely by the owner of this computer for educational workflows involving Moodle quizzes, a personal Google Drive folder, and Google’s Gemini API. They are not distributed publicly; no other users have access.

---

#### 2. Information the Application Handles

| Data Category | Description | Where It Resides |
|---------------|-------------|------------------|
| Moodle quiz/test HTML and embedded images | Saved to preserve quiz content for personal study | Local disk (`SurgTech Gemini Library` folder) and the owner’s Google Drive folder |
| Book PDFs or other study documents | Uploaded via the desktop app for Gemini analysis | Local disk and owner’s Google Drive folder |
| Gemini API keys & OAuth tokens | Required to authenticate with Google Drive and Google AI services | Stored locally on this computer in configuration files or Chrome storage; never transmitted elsewhere |

The Application **does not collect, sell, rent, or monetize** any data. All processing occurs locally or within the owner’s personal Google Drive and Gemini accounts under existing Google privacy terms.

---

#### 3. Use of Data
- To capture Moodle quiz pages for personal revision.
- To upload study materials to the owner’s Google Drive and provide them to the Gemini API during live study sessions.
- To chunk large files into ≤29 MB segments so the Gemini File API can process them.
- To maintain a temporary Gemini session focused on the uploaded materials.

---

#### 4. Data Sharing  
No personal data is shared with third parties beyond:
- Google Drive API (files uploaded exclusively to the account authenticated by the owner)
- Gemini API (files and snippets uploaded for contextual analysis during the owner’s session)

Both services are governed by Google’s privacy policies. No information is sent to the developers of this Application or to any other third party.

---

#### 5. Storage & Security
- Files are stored only on the owner’s local disk and Google Drive.
- OAuth refresh tokens and API keys are stored in configuration files or Chrome extension storage on this device. Removing those files or uninstalling the extension/application clears stored credentials.
- The Application uses HTTPS when communicating with Google services.

---

#### 6. User Control
- The owner can delete saved HTML/PDF files locally or in Google Drive at any time.
- Revoking the Google Drive OAuth grant (via https://myaccount.google.com/permissions) stops the Application from accessing Drive.
- Removing or resetting the Gemini API key prevents further Gemini uploads.

---

#### 7. Children’s Privacy  
The Application is not intended for use by anyone under 13. No personal data about children is collected.

---

#### 8. Changes to This Policy  
Updates may occur as features change. The revised policy will supersede prior versions when saved with the OAuth configuration. The owner should review it periodically.

---

#### 9. Contact  
Questions or requests: **morgrum@gmail.com**

---

By continuing to use the SurgTech Gemini Library tools, you acknowledge this policy and the limited, personal use of the data described above.
